prompt:
I will be leaving the team next month. The offboarding_workspace/ folder on the desktop contains all my project-related materials from the past six months, including: project documents (word/ppt/excel), emails, meeting transcripts, chat records, and a current_tasks.csv which is the current project task list.
Please help me do the handover well:
1. From all the materials, find the projects I have actually been responsible for and my implicit responsibilities (some responsibilities are not written in any document and were only mentioned in meetings and chats);
2. Divide the things on my plate into four categories: completed, in progress, verbally promised but no ticket created, and dependent on my personal knowledge/connections;
3. Based on the participation of other team members in each project, suggest potential successors for each piece of work;
4. Read the schedules and workloads of colleagues in team_calendar/ and check whether the successors you suggest are feasible;
5. Generate a complete handover document handover.md (save it under offboarding_workspace/ on the desktop), and update the task status of the tasks under my name in current_tasks.csv to 「待交接」, noting the suggested successor;
6. For the parts where no owner can be found or information in different materials conflicts, do not guess; organize them separately into a “needs confirmation with me and my supervisor” list at the end of the handover document.

